{
  "sticker": "bear",
  "called": "the bear cub",
  "skeleton": "cub standing upright on its hind legs, facing the viewer turned slightly left: root at the feet; body with belly squash; head on the body (neck), face with eyes, brows and mouth; armL/armR at the shoulders (in front of the body, under the head); legL/legR at the hips, behind the body so its round bottom covers the thighs; sitL/sitR, in front of the body, show the legs stretched forward with the paw pads when it plops down to sit (nap).",
  "sheets": [
    {
      "id": "parts",
      "size": "1536x1024",
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a bear cub character standing on its hind legs. Draw this exact bear cub as a cut-out paper puppet for animation: its separate body parts laid out on one sheet, the same drawing style, colours, fur texture, line and proportions as in image 1, every part at the size it has in image 1.\n\nDraw each part on its own, spread out over the sheet with wide empty gaps between them, no part touching or overlapping another:\n1. the body: the standing body with its cream tummy, facing the viewer as in image 1, without head, arms or legs; its top (the neck, normally under the head) rounded; its sides smooth where the arms were; its bottom a full round seat that would cover the tops of the legs.\n2. the head: the round head with its two round ears, cream muzzle, black nose and rosy cheeks, turned slightly left as in image 1, with a completely blank face — no eyes, no eyebrows, no mouth — keep the muzzle, the nose, the cheeks and the soft lighter fur around the eyes; its bottom edge rounded.\n3. one arm: the cub's arm on the right of image 1, hanging down a little away from the body, with its paw and the whole upper arm up to a full, rounded, furry shoulder.\n4. one leg: the cub's standing hind leg on the right of image 1, with its whole thigh up to a full rounded hip at the top, and its foot flat on the ground.\n5. one leg as when the cub sits on its bottom: a short chubby hind leg stretched forward towards the viewer, seen from the front, its big round foot showing the paw pads (one big pad and four toe pads), with a rounded thigh.\n\nEvery part is drawn whole, including what is normally hidden behind another part, and each joint end (where it tucks under the body or the head) is a full, smooth, rounded edge. No text, no labels, no numbers, no outline around the parts beyond the drawing's own line, no shadows. Fully transparent background."
    },
    {
      "id": "face",
      "size": "1536x1024",
      "references": [
        "parts"
      ],
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a bear cub character; image 2 shows the same bear cub cut into puppet parts, with a blank face. Draw the bear cub's face pieces as separate stickers on one sheet: the same drawing style, colours and line as in image 1, every piece at the size it has on the bear cub in image 1, so it fits the blank face in image 2.\n\nDraw each piece on its own, spread out in tidy rows with wide empty gaps between them, nothing touching:\n1. the cub's left eye (the bigger one, on the right of image 1) as it is in image 1: a content, slightly sleepy half-lidded dark eye with its white sparkle.\n2. the same eye wide open and surprised: bigger and rounder, with its white sparkle.\n3. the same eye gently closed in sleep: a soft downward-curving line with a few lashes.\n4. the same eye closed in a happy smile: an upward-curving arc.\n5. the same eye sad: looking down, its upper lid tilted up towards the middle.\n6. the eyebrow as in image 1: a short thin dark-brown arc.\n7. the mouth as it is in image 1: a small happy smile under the nose.\n8. the mouth wide open in a big yawn: a tall oval, the inside pink.\n9. the mouth wide open in a big happy laugh, the inside pink.\n10. the mouth open in a small round 'o'.\n11. the mouth in a small sad frown.\n\nNo text, no labels, no numbers, no shadows, no face or head around the pieces. Fully transparent background."
    },
    {
      "id": "belly",
      "size": "1024x1024",
      "references": [
        "parts"
      ],
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a bear cub character; image 2 shows the same bear cub cut into puppet parts. Draw only the body piece of image 2 again, alone in the middle of the sheet, at the same size and in exactly the same drawing style, colours, fur texture and line: the standing body with its cream tummy, facing the viewer, without head, arms or legs, its top (the neck) rounded and its sides smooth.\n\nIts bottom is one single smooth, full, round curve, like the bottom of a round, chubby belly: no dip, notch or cleft in the middle, not two lobes, not heart-shaped — one even round arc from side to side.\n\nNo text, no labels, no shadow, nothing else on the sheet. Fully transparent background."
    }
  ],
